{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451568-tips-for-playing-a-murderhobo-well","id":1451568,"title":"Tips for playing a \"murderhobo\" well?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-10T13:37:40-07:00","id":1451568,"title":"Tips for playing a \"murderhobo\" well?","content":"My next PC is aptly described as a murderhobo Vampire. Tzimisce, Soldier nature, extremely low opinion of humans. He doesn't hate them, much in the way humans don't hate cows or pigs. Ironically he is much more inhuman than edgy Sabbat Neonates who make a point of destroying humans and debasing their own humanity as far as possible - he doesn't think along those lines, he is something other than human.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I am very conscious of the fact that he lacks:<br /> <br /> - money<br /> - friends<br /> - official ties to the mortal world<br /> - a stable home<br /> - contacts<br /> - basic knowledge about certain human activities in modern nights<br /> <br /> What he does have:<br /> <br /> - a propensity for violence<br /> - a sociopathic disregard for humans<br /> - immense hunger<br /> - dangerous supernatural abilities<br /> - total commitment to his mission and whatever goals he currently strives to complete<br /> <br /> So my plan is to play up the anti-social element - not towards the party, who he considers to be other people, but towards the human world. He is unapologetically a Vampire, not a human with some condition, not a beautiful corpse, but a vampire who feeds and kills and lies.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any tips for playing such a character well? I think the most important hurdle is that I recognize that his behaviour will have consequences, whereas a typical murderhobo believes they can solve all their problems with a hammer OOC as well as IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T14:40:05-07:00","id":1451578,"title":"","content":"One thing you might do is roleplay the subtler aspects of being detached from humanity. I have neurological problems that make me somewhat detached, so let me give you an example of what that's like. A while back, I had to go to a public restroom. I got to the toilet stall, and found it was locked. I immediately noticed that the lock was kind of like a flathead screw. So I stuck my fingernail in, and turned it to unlock it. I opened the door and was startled by someone being in it and immediately shouting at me. So I closed the door. Other people in the bathroom, people whose existence I hadn't noticed until now, said things that basically called me an idiot. Apparently I had cut in line before unlocking the door.<br /> <br /> The point is, I had forgotten that human beings were a thing, forgotten that their behaviors and social norms were factors that had to be taken into account when interacting with the world. I saw a physical obstacle to getting what I wanted, and solved it via purely physical means. Only when people started yelling at me did I remember these things. And I'm just some regular human being with mild neurological issues. It would be worse for something actually inhuman.<br /> <br /> So basically, roleplay what it is like to have to constantly remind yourself that you are not alone in a world of purely physical obstacles in need of physical solutions. That doesn't have to mean violence. I struggle with this routinely without being the least bit violent. Most often, it means a constant awkwardness and subtle creepiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T15:05:09-07:00","id":1451582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451568-tips-for-playing-a-murderhobo-well?p=1451578#post1451578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing you might do is roleplay the subtler aspects of being detached from humanity. I have neurological problems that make me somewhat detached, so let me give you an example of what that's like. A while back, I had to go to a public restroom. I got to the toilet stall, and found it was locked. I immediately noticed that the lock was kind of like a flathead screw. So I stuck my fingernail in, and turned it to unlock it. I opened the door and was startled by someone being in it and immediately shouting at me. So I closed the door. Other people in the bathroom, people whose existence I hadn't noticed until now, said things that basically called me an idiot. Apparently I had cut in line before unlocking the door.<br /> <br /> The point is, I had forgotten that human beings were a thing, forgotten that their behaviors and social norms were factors that had to be taken into account when interacting with the world. I saw a physical obstacle to getting what I wanted, and solved it via purely physical means. Only when people started yelling at me did I remember these things. And I'm just some regular human being with mild neurological issues. It would be worse for something actually inhuman.<br /> <br /> So basically, roleplay what it is like to have to constantly remind yourself that you are not alone in a world of purely physical obstacles in need of physical solutions. That doesn't have to mean violence. I struggle with this routinely without being the least bit violent. Most often, it means a constant awkwardness and subtle creepiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the personal example, that's really helpful. I'm reminded of a thing from a book where the protagonist is asked what's in a box of smarties. He guesses smarties, and is shown it's actually a pencil. His mother then enters the room after this and the teacher asks what the mother would guess is inside. He says a pencil. Perfect demonstration of him not intuitively understanding that other people are separate to him.<br /> <br /> So for my Tzimisce, it could be stuff like not understanding that people (humans) have their own motivations and feelings that go beyond survival and base instincts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T16:55:58-07:00","id":1451593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451568-tips-for-playing-a-murderhobo-well#post1451568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any tips for playing such a character well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not doing this as a Tzimisce. Unless you're <i>planning</i> on their clan flaw playing a part in a chronicle for perhaps the first time in Vampire history, while simultaneously begging your ST to fuck you six ways from Sunday with it.<br /> <br /> It's perhaps just me, but if a player came to me with a character concept with quite that stunning lack of foresight I'd allow it with the biggest shit-eating grin on the planet and singing the &quot;Golden Ticket&quot; song from Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T02:18:22-07:00","id":1451622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451568-tips-for-playing-a-murderhobo-well?p=1451593#post1451593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not doing this as a Tzimisce. Unless you're <i>planning</i> on their clan flaw playing a part in a chronicle for perhaps the first time in Vampire history, while simultaneously begging your ST to fuck you six ways from Sunday with it.<br /> <br /> It's perhaps just me, but if a player came to me with a character concept with quite that stunning lack of foresight I'd allow it with the biggest shit-eating grin on the planet and singing the &quot;Golden Ticket&quot; song from Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might as well reveal this here since none of the players use this forum - he's a blood brother, his &quot;sire&quot; is actually his creator. He presents as Tzimisce so it's relevant to his character, but he is not truly a member of the clan.<br /> <br /> Since he was born a vampire, and has no memories of any human life, that's part of the reason he is the way he is. He doesn't know what it's like to be human, so he has misconceptions that even the most jaded and inhumane elder could never have. Once upon a time that elder giggled and played with other children, but that doesn't apply to someone with no human memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-11-2021, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T10:02:44-07:00","id":1451683,"title":"","content":"I feel like it'd be fun to have a ghoul around to constantly mother you and make sure you won't get in too much trouble. The character would last longer, at least. <br /> <br /> Invest in Obfuscate, perhaps Auspex. Stealth and larceny will get you more kills than elite combat skills. perhaps investigation if you want to be smart about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T02:36:46-07:00","id":1451822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451568-tips-for-playing-a-murderhobo-well?p=1451683#post1451683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it'd be fun to have a ghoul around to constantly mother you and make sure you won't get in too much trouble. The character would last longer, at least.<br /> <br /> Invest in Obfuscate, perhaps Auspex. Stealth and larceny will get you more kills than elite combat skills. perhaps investigation if you want to be smart about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting a Ghoul would be an intelligent move, but he won't do that unless his opinion of humans changes considerably IC.<br /> <br /> I should note that this isn't a case of &quot;how can I win the game&quot;, more &quot;how do I make this character as compelling and interesting as possible&quot;. I do have some good stealth capabilities though, Dex 4 with a spec in ambushes, Stealth 3, Celerity 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T04:49:48-07:00","id":1451828,"title":"","content":"Aight, but a compelling character needs to not suspend suspension of disbelief when he makes it past the first few murders. When you make a stupid-evil character, the Storyteller has two extremes; someone makes it their mission to take you down and they're unreasonably good at it, or the law is handed an idiot ball because the storyteller doesn't want to upset you, the player, by hurting your character too much. You'd ideally like them to be rational about it, but when you get into stuff that makes the storyteller emotional, their perception is at the very least coloured. <br /> <br /> -A Ghoul works for the character if that ghoul is &quot;special&quot; and the character's <i>weird </i>about the ghoul. Not knowing how stuff works is scary; a parental figure to get weirdly attached to is fun RP. You could have the character consider their ghoul something not-human, though they might be very ordinary, in the eyes of the Blood Brother, they're a divine figure. <br /> <br /> But, other stuff to recommend: <br /> <br /> Disproportionate responses to mild inconveniences. <br /> Expecting other people to read your mind, or put down whatever they're doing to prioritize you. If they don't, it's personal. <br /> Not doing the same for other people, or doing the same for other people and expecting a reward. <br /> Remembering only parts of the story, and bringing it up on occasion. &quot;Remember that time you kicked me? You caused a bruise! You kicked me you monster!&quot; &quot;you kicked me six to eight times and only after getting to that point did I kick back, and I kicked back only once&quot; &quot;YOU KICKED ME TWICE!!! &quot;YOU KICKED ME SIX TIMES&quot; &quot;Why did I kick you?&quot; &quot;because I didn't clean something&quot; and then have this conversation repeat every few months, with the aggrieved person always forgetting the parts where they were in the wrong. <br /> Taunting your victims.<br /> Acting super-righteous about everything. <br /> Believe you're on a mission from God. <br /> Getting sexually excited about murder<br /> <br /> ...and so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}